# zzyc-owner-skip-launch-constraints.patch

#
# Root acceptance without the owner-root trust switch: the reference record shows the
# unverified-root configuration is the one where AMFI accepts the dyld shared cache and
# launchd's libSystem resolves, while CONFIG_XNU_OWNER_ROOT_TRUST makes AMFI insist on owner
# signatures the IPSW's cache does not carry.  This patch stops the bsd_init panic as long as
# the eMMC driver vouches for the mounted root, and leaves AMFI's policy alone.
#
# dandelion-root-authorize.patch
#
# AMFI's exec answer can still refuse an Apple-signed binary on an owner-verified volume even
# though the trust cache module loaded.  sheng-skip-cs=1 clears imgp->ip_mac_return, which is
# what the reference ports record ("clearing that answer makes exec_activate_image return 0").
# The argument is off by default: a properly trusted image never needs it.
#
dandelion-skip-cs.patch
